{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json, math, statistics\nfrom pathlib import Path\nstrategy=json.loads(Path('paper_strategy.json').read_text())\npaper=json.loads(Path('paper_data.json').read_text())\nmemo=Path('paper_strategy.md').read_text()\nexpected={'status','selected_prompt_family','recommended_title','central_question','central_thesis','narrative_rationale','prior_paper_story_status','edit_framing_decision','staged_input_impact','method_groups','results_focus','figure_plan','figure_specs','supplementary_plan','forbidden_headings','forbidden_phrases','notes_for_writer','failure_reason'}\nassert set(strategy)==expected\nassert strategy['status']=='ready' and strategy['selected_prompt_family']=='paper_standalone'\nassert strategy['recommended_title'] in memo\nassert strategy['central_question'] in memo\nassert strategy['failure_reason']==''\nassert strategy['prior_paper_story_status'] in {'preserved','broadened','recentered','rejected'}\nassert strategy['supplementary_plan']['purpose'] and strategy['supplementary_plan']['planned_subsections']\nfor section in strategy['supplementary_plan']['planned_subsections']:\n assert section['heading'] and section['grounded_content'] and section['source_ids']\n for source in section['source_ids']:\n  assert source in paper['grounding_sources'], source\n  assert source in memo, source\nfor method in strategy['method_groups']:\n assert method['role'] in {'baseline','proposed','ablation','supporting'}\n assert method['name'] and method['include_reason']\nassert len(strategy['figure_plan'])==len(strategy['figure_specs'])==3\nassert sum(fig['preferred_generator']=='generate-concept-figure' for fig in strategy['figure_specs'])==1\nfor figure in strategy['figure_specs']:\n assert figure['figure_id'] in memo\n assert figure['required'] and not figure['allow_progression']\n assert figure['max_panels']<=4 and figure['max_categories_per_panel']<=6 and figure['max_series_per_panel']<=4\n assert figure['preferred_span']=='full_width' and figure['target_width_fraction']==1.0\n assert figure['layout_rationale']\nfinal=paper['final_evaluation']; sources=paper['grounding_sources']\nassert final['status']==sources['final.qualification.status']['value']=='completed'\nassert final['outcome']==sources['final.qualification.outcome']['value']=='qualified'\nassert sources['final.qualification.correct']['value'] is True\nassert paper.get('downstream_study') is None and paper['ablation_studies']==[]\nepisodes=final['evaluation_evidence']['episodes']; assert len(episodes)==400\nassert len({row['seed'] for row in episodes})==400\nsummary=episodes[0]['solution']['summary']; assert len(summary)==7\nassert summary['gene_expression']['paired_widths']['ppi_plus_plus']['difference_interval'][1]<0\nassert all(row['paired_widths']['ppi_plus_plus']['difference_interval'][0]>0 for case,row in summary.items() if case\"'!='\"'gene_expression')\ncoverage=[statistics.mean(episode['solution']['cases'][case]['coverage'] for episode in episodes) for case in summary]\nassert min(coverage)==0.95 and max(coverage)==0.98\nassert math.isclose(statistics.mean(coverage),final['metrics']['empirical_coverage'])\nrare=[episode['solution']['cases']['rare_outcome']['observations'] for episode in episodes]\nassert sum(row['ppi_plus_plus'][0]==row['ppi_plus_plus'][1] for row in rare)==5\nassert statistics.mean(row['baseline_coverage']['ppi_plus_plus'] for row in rare)==0.92\nassert summary['rare_outcome']['coverage_intervals']['ppi_plus_plus'][0]<0.95<summary['rare_outcome']['coverage_intervals']['ppi_plus_plus'][1]\nassert not Path('paper.tex').exists() and not Path('claims_grounding.json').exists()\nassert not list(Path('figures').iterdir())\nprint('PASS: strategy schema, mirrored title/question/source IDs, figure budgets and geometry, qualification independence, all-condition evidence, rare-outcome audit, and stage boundaries.')\nprint('No final-paper validation or experimental execution performed.')\nPY\npython .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --write-conclusions --conclusions-md /workspace/investigation/conclusions.md --conclusions-history-jsonl /workspace/investigation/conclusions_history.jsonl --gate-trigger d --gate-reason 'Qualify the source-only recommendations by separating final measured conditional method performance from still-unidentified component effects and unproved coverage.' --conclusions-text 'Audit cross-fit studentization for fold-specific offset invariance: weighted within-fold residual variances and variance after combining shared-pool controls preserve cancellation, but overlapping learned folds still require explicit stability assumptions. Keep training-only zero/affine/nonlinear risk comparisons separate from selection of completed intervals, and apply the finite-unlabeled-noise penalty once. Use the frozen selected risk-adaptive method and matched final endpoints for scientific comparisons: the empirical gene-expression source supports a width benefit against both PPI references, while every other evaluated condition is wider than PPI++. Preserve this conditional boundary rather than asserting universal narrowing or attributing the gain to nonlinear calibration without component ablations. Treat smooth covariance stacking as an exploratory alternative, not the final method or an established improvement; near ties and collinearity remain useful diagnostics. Show per-condition coverage uncertainty alongside width, and do not let observed nominal attainment, operational qualification, an unbiased deterministic variance formula, or an unreturned internal certificate stand in for validity of the reported interval. Audit zero-width rare-event references using paired differences and ratios of means rather than interpreting capped episode ratios as ordinary width effects. Keep empirical-source resampling distinct from external-population validation, and quarantine unscreened recent bibliography candidates under the restricted-literature policy.'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
